m+Gordon+BYE+BYE&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2024 Matador"]}, {"t": 21120, "time": "05:52:00", "artist": "Arcuda", "title": "Road To Atlantis", "conf": "low", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1313847691", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Arcuda+Road+To+Atlantis&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2017 LKAB RECORDINGS"]}], "counts": {"high": 0, "mid": 12, "low": 13}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:04:56", "end": "00:05:16", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:05:32", "end": "00:06:02", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:06:40", "end": "00:07:11", "text": ""}, {"start": "00:07:39", "end": "00:08:50", "text": "Thank you."}, {"start": "00:33:54", "end": "00:34:17", "text": "We'll see you next time."}, {"start": "00:34:23", "end": "00:34:52", "text": "We'll see you next time."}, {"start": "00:37:19", "end": "00:38:23", "text": "We'll be right back."}, {"start": "00:46:03", "end": "00:46:20", "text": "I've never had a minute to worry the freaks ain't gonna hurt, stop sending. I want a hundred percent publishing, so I'm gonna DIY. I know some don't care about the grime scene, but I'm gonna till I die. I got beats and flow, stadium show, so I'm here doing a ride."}, {"start": "01:30:40", "end": "01:31:24", "text": "To whom did Gabriel show tonight the inward path of scarlet secrets? Outside this flowing Sydney nightclub where we stood with quiet secrets, in a line that stretched within where my friends wait with secrets, letting peachy soju drip like layers of tongues, all losing secrets. Friends inside will see me there Ask the DJ to play his secrets Between his sets to me he whispers Each song I play is filled with secrets Junaid, the soul of souls is ours And his liquor bears its secrets The scarlet taste of a Sydney night Is a scarlet youth drenched in secrets"}, {"start": "01:31:51", "end": "01:32:45", "text": "Last summer I was seventeen, and electric, and hanging in that hot midday air, where you came to me on the breeze, so close with the smell of your steel earrings, so close with that flesh on a warm day, on a cotton sheet, on a cool finger that traced my doorline, traced my lips, came to the wetness of my furrowed brava, and back to my needing heart. Listen to what stillness you have made in me. Come kiss my shoulder blades like the sweet concrete of the sea. So far from where this longing was really into me, this pulse, this boyhood you have found between wetware and website, this wetness, this machine, this memory that will take you to an electric ocean, strung up like the summer sky."}, {"start": "02:50:50", "end": "02:51:09", "text": "And then, yeah, girls said I'm my favorite. I'm heard up by the way Europe, we got exotica's here. No, I don't know how to hear it. Step up and be a hero. Come back from the side of my pocket, my money is European. Air I'm in on my sweater, I'm overseas being famous. Cranked inside of my juice. Cranked inside of my shoes. After the show, signing a shoe. Drip, I'm covered in goo. Get a pose like I'm in a photo. They like to. It's hard to get a hold of you. Me and rap."}, {"start": "03:09:54", "end": "03:10:13", "text": "Temenos, a piece of landmark off from common uses and assigned as an official domain, especially to a king, chief, or god. A sacred circle where one can be oneself without fear."}, {"start": "03:12:51", "end": "03:13:30", "text": "A lot of times you can't solve them and they'll be solved. The most famous one will be solving dreams. The most famous one is Kikuli's benzene ring. He fell asleep in front of his fire and he dreamt of the hoopsnake, the uroboros, the snake with its tail and so on. And when he woke up he realized, oh, it's a ring. But that raises the question as to why, you know, if your subconscious has solved this problem and is ready to tell you, why wouldn't it? We don't know, but it may have to do with the subconscious being older than language."}, {"start": "03:41:44", "end": "03:42:04", "text": "I could be the sun, be some other one I could touch the earth, see, feel earth, wind, fire I could hold my breath for another time I could see gold, precious moss, so real time I can find a handsome landscape It holds no present, synthesis too"}, {"start": "03:42:11", "end": "03:42:29", "text": "I could frame the flame, hold the smog of another day Maybe I'm the one, just the sky at some purple I can find a handsome landscape There's water on the rock again, grease sweeps over me"}, {"start": "04:58:31", "end": "04:58:59", "text": ""}, {"start": "05:57:12", "end": "05:58:25", "text": "Picture yourself being 10 years old and having visions stuck in prison because of stories that were told around you when you was younger. Now that's all you could see. Thinking more than lucky that could be me. See my uncle on TV for a prison escape and at the age of 16 I thought I'd seen my fate. Always thought it was inevitable, what more can I say? To this day I get the feeling they might lock me away. I'm a black man living in this country where it's normal to be sent to a place where my people make almost 50%. That's half of the populations in our prisons today We only make up 3% of this country Ain't that a shame? Yeah, that's fucked up Men ain't got us cuffed up People out here dying, but we'd rather fill our cups up Fathers leaving sons and turn around and say it's tough love Making up excuses, spitting rubbish like a dump truck But am I being realistic For trying to get this message to the ones that might have missed it? We only get one life, so why risk it? Man, fuck being a statistic It's time to change the way we see the world But more important, it's time to change the way we see ourselves How we supposed to spread our wings before we see his help We are kings and we are queens before we're anything else It's got me thinking while I'm making this We plan funerals before we"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "-1:59:51"}, "track": {"title": "Integrity", "artists": [{"name": "Kamasi Washington"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:26:18"}, "track": {"title": "See (feat. Sophia Al-Maria & Ben Vince)", "artists": [{"name": "Moin"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:48:00"}, "track": {"title": "Tuna Salad Samba", "artists": [{"name": "Leo Nankawa"}, {"name": "Saiming & Bpm Music Collective"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:53:19"}, "track": {"title": "Temporary", "artists": [{"name": "Jabu"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:04:27"}, "track": {"title": "Uneasy", "artists": [{"name": "Dregs"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:17:13"}, "track": {"title": "Bruce Lee", "artists": [{"name": "Underworld"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:24:42"}, "track": {"title": "Interrupted Exception Coding Music", "artists": [{"name": "Video Game Raps"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "01:30:53"}, "track": {"title": "Set Me Free (Rising Star Remix)", "artists": [{"name": "Armin van Buuren & SACHA"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enable